  "question": {
    "text": "A point charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;is placed at some distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;away from the centre of a grounded conducting sphere of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>, as shown in the figure.&nbsp;The charge that flows from the earth to the sphere is<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0028_9b7932e618b3.jpg\" style=\"height: 146px; width: 200px;\" />"
  },
